---
layout: base.njk
title: Pledges
description: Promises made in Malta's manifestos, budgets and announcements, labelled by whether they can be measured and how they are progressing, with an as-of date, who made them, when, and which pledges overlap.
permalink: /pledges/
---
{%- import "macros.njk" as m -%}
{%- set P = mizien.pledges -%}
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Pledges</li></ol>
</nav>

<article class="page prose-page pledges-page">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Pledges</p>
    <h1>Pledges</h1>
    <p class="lead">A pledge is a promise of future action, so it gets a label instead of a verdict: whether it can be
      measured and, if so, how it is going. Every label carries an <em>as of</em> date, the date of the evidence behind it.</p>
  </header>

  <p class="see-also">{% icon "links" %}<span><a href="/explore/?group=pledges">See the pledges over time in Explore</a>: one lane per
    party and one for commitments made in office, each pledge on the date it was made with a bar to its deadline, and a line
    from a pledge to the earlier one it carries forward (red where the earlier one was not met).</span></p>

  {%- set PG = mizien.pledge_grid %}
  {%- macro pq(x) -%}<a class="pg-p" href="{{ x.path }}" data-claim="{{ x.id }}" title="{{ x.id }} {{ x.title }}: {{ x.pledge_status }}"><span class="pg-sq" style="background:{{ x.pledge_colour }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ x.id }}<span class="visually-hidden"> ({{ x.pledge_status }})</span></a>{%- endmacro %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-grid">
    <h2 id="h-grid">By election and party</h2>
    <p>Every party that contested each general election, in alphabetical order. A cell gives the number of pledges listed
      from its programme, the pledges checked so far, the listed pledges linked to another pledge, and any outlier.
      Commitments made in office have their own column.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="pgrid">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Election</span></th>
        {%- for c in PG.columns %}<th scope="col" title="{{ c.full }}">{{ c.name }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {%- for r in PG.rows %}
        <tr><th scope="row">{{ r.year }}<span class="small"> election</span></th>
        {%- for cell in r.cells %}
          {%- if not cell.contested %}<td class="pg-na"><span class="small">did not contest</span></td>
          {%- elif cell.status == "office" %}<td class="pg-office">{% for x in cell.checked %}{{ pq(x) }} {% else %}<span class="small">none checked</span>{% endfor %}</td>
          {%- elif cell.status != "listed" %}<td class="pg-none"><a href="/pledges/#h-manifestos">{{ cell.status | capitalize }}</a></td>
          {%- else %}<td><a class="pg-n" href="/pledges/manifestos/#{{ cell.anchor }}">{{ cell.listed }}</a> <span class="small">listed</span>
            {%- if cell.checked.length %}<br>{% for x in cell.checked %}{{ pq(x) }} {% endfor %}{% endif %}
            {%- if cell.linked %}<br><span class="small">{{ cell.linked }} linked</span>{% endif %}
            {%- if cell.recycled %}<br><a class="pg-flag" href="#outlier-recycled">{{ cell.recycled }} promised again</a>{% endif %}
            {%- if cell.dropped %}<br><a class="pg-flag" href="#outlier-dropped">{{ cell.dropped }} dropped</a>{% endif %}</td>
          {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}</tr>
      {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <ul class="pgrid-key" aria-label="Key">{% for l in mizien.pledge_labels %}<li><span class="pg-sq" style="background:{{ l.colour }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ l.name }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
    {%- if PG.other.length %}
    <p class="small">Also checked, outside these columns: {% for x in PG.other %}{{ pq(x) }} ({{ x.kind_label | lower }}, {{ x.cycle_label }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  {%- set TM = mizien.pledge_topic_matrix %}
  {%- if TM.cycles %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-topics">
    <h2 id="h-topics">What each programme promised, by subject</h2>
    <p>Every pledge in the manifesto list placed under one of {{ TM.topics.length }} subjects, a taxonomy drawn up from the
      pledges themselves (each placement read by a person). The deeper the shade, the more pledges; hover over a number
      for its subtopics, or press it to read the pledges. A party with more pledges on a subject has not necessarily
      promised more: programmes differ in length and in how finely they split a promise.</p>
    {%- for c in TM.cycles %}
    <h3 class="pt-h">{{ c.year }} election</h3>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="ptopics">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Subject</th>
        {%- for p in c.parties %}<th scope="col">{{ p.name }}<span class="small"> · {{ p.total }}</span></th>{% endfor %}
        <th scope="col" class="pt-all">All</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {%- for r in c.rows %}
        <tr><th scope="row">{{ r.topic }}</th>
        {%- for cell in r.cells %}
          {%- if cell.n %}<td style="--s: {{ cell.shade }}"{% if cell.shade > 0.5 %} class="pt-dark"{% endif %}><a href="/pledges/manifestos/?topic={{ r.slug }}#{{ cell.party }}-{{ c.id }}" title="{{ cell.sub }}">{{ cell.n }}</a></td>
          {%- else %}<td class="pt-0"><span aria-label="none">·</span></td>{% endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
        <td class="pt-all">{{ r.total }}</td></tr>
      {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </section>
  {%- endif %}

  {%- set SM = mizien.pledge_similar %}
  {%- if SM.parties %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-similar">
    <h2 id="h-similar">Promised again? Similar wording in {{ SM.first_year }} and {{ SM.last_year }}</h2>
    <p>For the parties with a programme at both elections, each {{ SM.last_year }} pledge is compared with the party's own
      {{ SM.first_year }} programme. <strong>Found automatically and not yet reviewed:</strong> similar wording is a lead,
      not a link. A pledge can carry an earlier one forward in new words (and score low), or share words with a different
      promise (and score high). Only a person's reading makes it a link, which then appears in the grid above and on the
      claim pages.</p>
    <div class="sim-bars">
    {%- for p in SM.parties %}
      <div class="sim-row"><span class="sim-name">{{ p.name }}</span>
        <span class="sim-bar" role="img" aria-label="{{ p.name }}: of {{ p.total }} pledges in {{ SM.last_year }}, {{ p.strong }} with strongly similar wording in {{ SM.first_year }}, {{ p.possible }} possibly similar, {{ p.unmatched }} none found">
          {%- if p.strong %}<i class="s2" style="flex: {{ p.strong }}"></i>{% endif %}{% if p.possible %}<i class="s1" style="flex: {{ p.possible }}"></i>{% endif %}{% if p.unmatched %}<i class="s0" style="flex: {{ p.unmatched }}"></i>{% endif %}</span>
        <span class="sim-n small"><b>{{ p.strong }}</b> strong · <b>{{ p.possible }}</b> possible · {{ p.unmatched }} none, of {{ p.total }}</span></div>
    {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <ul class="sim-key small" aria-hidden="true"><li><i class="s2"></i>Strongly similar wording</li><li><i class="s1"></i>Possibly similar</li><li><i class="s0"></i>None found among the closest candidates</li></ul>
    <p class="small">How close two programmes' wording is depends on how they are written as well as on what they promise.
      The Nationalist Party's {{ SM.last_year }} programme was published as web chapters, in a different structure from its
      {{ SM.first_year }} document, and wording alone cannot tell a promise rewritten from a new one. These counts do not
      measure how many promises a party repeated, kept or dropped.</p>

    <details class="sim-topics">
      <summary>By subject</summary>
      <div class="sim-bars">
      {%- for t in SM.topics %}{% if t.total %}
        <div class="sim-row"><span class="sim-name">{{ t.topic }}</span>
          <span class="sim-bar" role="img" aria-label="{{ t.topic }}: {{ t.strong }} strong, {{ t.possible }} possible, {{ t.unmatched }} none, of {{ t.total }}">
            {%- if t.strong %}<i class="s2" style="flex: {{ t.strong }}"></i>{% endif %}{% if t.possible %}<i class="s1" style="flex: {{ t.possible }}"></i>{% endif %}{% if t.unmatched %}<i class="s0" style="flex: {{ t.unmatched }}"></i>{% endif %}</span>
          <span class="sim-n small"><b>{{ t.strong }}</b> · <b>{{ t.possible }}</b> · {{ t.unmatched }} of {{ t.total }}</span></div>
      {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </details>

    {%- for p in SM.parties %}{% if p.pairs.length %}
    <details class="sim-pairs">
      <summary>{{ p.name }}: the {{ p.pairs.length }} strongly similar pairs</summary>
      <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="claims">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ SM.first_year }} programme</th><th scope="col">{{ SM.last_year }} programme</th><th scope="col">Subject</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {%- for x in p.pairs %}
          <tr><td><a href="/pledges/manifestos/#{{ x.before.id }}">No. {{ x.before.number }}</a> {{ x.before.summary }}</td>
            <td><a href="/pledges/manifestos/#{{ x.after.id }}">No. {{ x.after.number }}</a> {{ x.after.summary }}{% if x.confirmed %}<br><span class="small">Linked by a person.</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="small">{{ x.topic }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>
    </details>
    {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
  </section>
  {%- endif %}

  <section aria-labelledby="h-labels">
    <h2 id="h-labels">The labels</h2>
    <dl class="pledge-labels">
      {%- for l in mizien.pledge_labels %}
      <div><dt><span class="badge {{ l.slug }} v-{{ l.slug }}">{{ l.name }}</span></dt><dd>{{ l.meaning | mdInline | safe }}</dd></div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
    <p class="small">A check of a pledge alone shows only its label. A check that also tests factual statements keeps its
      verdict for those and shows the label beside it. Decided on 5 October 2026; see the Pledges section of
      <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/methodology/verdict-scale.md#pledges">the verdict scale</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="h-list">
    <h2 id="h-list">Pledges checked so far</h2>
    {%- if P.length %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="claims pledge-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Pledge</th><th scope="col">Made by</th><th scope="col">Made in</th><th scope="col">Deadline</th><th scope="col">Label</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {%- for x in P %}
        <tr><td>{{ m.claim(x) }}<br><span class="small">{{ x.pledge.target }}</span></td>
          <td>{% for b in x.pledge.made_by %}<a href="{{ b.path }}">{{ b.name }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
          <td>{{ x.pledge.vehicle }}{% if x.pledge.made_on %}<br><span class="small">{{ x.pledge.made_on }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{{ x.pledge.deadline or "none stated" }}{% if x.pledge.term_end %}<br><span class="small">term ended {{ x.pledge.term_end }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
          <td><span class="badge v-{{ x.pledge.slug }}">{{ x.pledge.status }}</span><br><span class="small">as of {{ x.pledge.as_of }}</span>
            {%- if x.verdict %}<br><span class="small">verdict on the facts: {{ x.verdict }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
      {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    {%- else %}
    <p>No pledge is labelled yet.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  {%- set OL = mizien.outlier_list %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-outliers">
    <h2 id="h-outliers">Outliers</h2>
    <p>The usual chain runs from a campaign promise to a commitment in office to an outcome. An outlier breaks that chain.
      Each is stated as a finding with the record it rests on, never inferred from a gap, and never about motive. The
      rules are in the Outliers part of <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/methodology/verdict-scale.md#pledges">the verdict scale</a>.</p>
    {%- set types = [
      ["recycled", "Recycled", "The same promise made again in a later election while the earlier one was not met. Applies to every party."],
      ["drift", "Drift", "A commitment linked to an earlier promise, but changed from it: a target lowered, a deadline moved, the scope narrowed or the measure changed."],
      ["unanchored", "Unanchored", "A government commitment with no earlier pledge behind it. Shown only after a recorded search of the manifestos."],
      ["dropped", "Dropped", "A campaign pledge of the governing party with no follow-up in office. Shown only after the legislature has ended and a search is recorded."]
    ] %}
    {%- for t in types %}
    {%- set items = OL | where("type", t[0]) %}
    <h3 id="outlier-{{ t[0] }}">{{ t[1] }} <span class="small">({{ items.length }})</span></h3>
    <p class="small">{{ t[2] }}</p>
    {%- if items.length %}
    <ul class="outliers">
      {%- for o in items %}
      <li>{% if o.claim %}{{ m.claim(o.claim) }}{% else %}<a href="/pledges/manifestos/#{{ o.manifesto.id }}">{{ o.manifesto.name }}</a>
        <span class="small">({{ o.manifesto.summary | replace(r/\.$/, "") }}; in the manifesto list, not checked)</span>{% endif %}
        <br>{{ o.text | mdInline | safe }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- elif t[0] == "dropped" %}
    <p class="none">None recorded yet. The 2022–26 legislature has ended; the check of the governing party's 2022
      pledges for a follow-up in office has not been done.</p>
    {%- elif t[0] == "unanchored" %}
    <p class="none">None recorded yet. A commitment is listed here only after a recorded search finds no earlier pledge.</p>
    {%- else %}
    <p class="none">None recorded yet.</p>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- set fw = OL | where("type", "follows") %}
    {%- if fw.length %}
    <h3 id="carried-forward">Carried forward <span class="small">({{ fw.length }})</span></h3>
    <p class="small">Not outliers: a commitment that takes forward an earlier pledge, as recorded. Shown so that the chains
      can be followed, and on <a href="/explore/?group=pledges">the pledges timeline in Explore</a>.</p>
    <ul class="outliers">
      {%- for o in fw %}
      <li>{% if o.claim %}{{ m.claim(o.claim) }}{% else %}<a href="/pledges/manifestos/#{{ o.manifesto.id }}">{{ o.manifesto.name }}</a>{% endif %}
        <br>{{ o.text | mdInline | safe }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  {%- set PF = mizien.pledge_flows %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-flows">
    <h2 id="h-flows">From promise to outcome</h2>
    {%- if PF.length %}
    <p>For each programme whose follow-up check is complete: what happened in office to every pledge listed from it, and,
      where the commitment was checked, its label. Drawn to scale.</p>
    {%- for f in PF %}
    <figure class="pflow">
      <figcaption><b>{{ f.name }}</b> · {{ f.total }} pledges listed · follow-up checked {{ f.checked }}</figcaption>
      <div class="table-scroll">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 {{ f.chart.width }} {{ f.chart.height }}" width="{{ f.chart.width }}" height="{{ f.chart.height }}" role="img" aria-label="{{ f.name }}: {% for c in f.counts %}{{ c.label }} {{ c.n }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}">
        {%- for l in f.chart.links %}<path d="{{ l.d }}" fill="{{ l.colour }}" opacity=".45"><title>{{ l.title }}</title></path>{% endfor %}
        {%- for n in f.chart.nodes %}<rect x="{{ n.x }}" y="{{ n.y }}" width="{{ n.w }}" height="{{ n.h }}" rx="2" fill="{{ n.colour }}"></rect>
        <text x="{{ n.lx }}" y="{{ n.ly }}" text-anchor="{{ n.anchor }}">{{ n.label }}</text>{% endfor %}
      </svg>
      </div>
    </figure>
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- else %}
    <p class="none">Not drawn yet. A programme's flow appears here once every pledge listed from it has been checked for a
      follow-up in office, so that a pledge not yet checked is never shown as if it had been dropped. No programme has
      been fully checked so far.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  {%- set MC = mizien.manifesto_coverage %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-manifestos">
    <h2 id="h-manifestos">The manifesto list</h2>
    <p>So that pledges can be linked across elections, Miżien keeps a light list of the pledges in each programme: the
      whole of every environment chapter and every climate and energy chapter, for every party that contested the
      election, to the same scope. Each is a summary in our own words with its number and page. Most have not been
      checked; a listed pledge carries no label until it is.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="claims mp-coverage">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Election</th><th scope="col">Party</th><th scope="col">Programme</th><th scope="col">Pledges listed</th><th scope="col">With a target</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      {%- for c in MC %}
        <tr><td>{{ c.cycle }}</td><td>{{ c.party_name }}</td>
          <td>{% if c.status == "listed" %}<a href="/pledges/manifestos/#{{ c.anchor }}">{{ c.document }}</a>{% else %}<span class="small">{{ c.status | capitalize }}. {{ c.searched }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
          <td>{{ c.rows if c.status == "listed" else "–" }}</td><td>{{ c.measurable if c.status == "listed" else "–" }}</td></tr>
      {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Counts differ because programmes differ in length and layout, not in scope. "With a target": the
      pledge states a quantity, date or deadline that could be checked. <a href="/pledges/manifestos/">Browse the list</a>.</p>
  </section>

  {%- set overlapping = P | having("overlaps.length") %}
  {%- if overlapping.length %}
  <section aria-labelledby="h-overlaps">
    <h2 id="h-overlaps">Overlapping pledges</h2>
    <p>Pledges overlap when they are listed as overlapping, share a theme, or are on the same subtopic. Overlapping
      pledges are worth reading together, for example when two parties promise to tackle the same problem.</p>
    <ul class="linked-bodies">
      {%- for x in overlapping %}
      <li><p class="lb-name">{{ m.claim(x) }}</p>
        {%- for o in x.overlaps %}<p class="lb-why">Overlaps {{ m.claim(o) }}: {{ o.why | join("; ") }}.</p>{% endfor %}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}
</article>
